      "title": "Number Spiral",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": false,
      "solution": "n = int(input())\n\ngrid = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\ntop = 0\nbottom = n - 1\nleft = 0\nright = n - 1\n\nvalue = 1\n\nwhile left <= right and top <= bottom:\n\n    for x in range(left, right + 1):\n        grid[top][x] = value\n        value += 1\n    top += 1\n\n    for y in range(top, bottom + 1):\n        grid[y][right] = value\n        value += 1\n    right -= 1\n\n    if top <= bottom:\n        for x in range(right, left - 1, -1):\n            grid[bottom][x] = value\n            value += 1\n        bottom -= 1\n\n    if left <= right:\n        for y in range(bottom, top - 1, -1):\n            grid[y][left] = value\n            value += 1\n        left += 1\n\nfor row in grid:\n    print(*row)",
      "statement": "Given an integer N, print an N × N grid filled with numbers from 1 to N² in a clockwise spiral starting from the top-left corner.",
